0..74 Comment "// What does not cross, refused where it would. A migration\'s result comes"
75..148 Comment "// back to the world the migration left, and only what is mobile and open"
149..225 Comment "// comes back: an unmarked abstract type stays with its seal, a handle stays"
226..303 Comment "// when what it holds is not open, and a suspended computation stays where it"
304..317 Comment "// would run."
319..393 Comment "// The operator\'s and the seat\'s worlds, and the seat\'s sealed side of the"
394..438 Comment "// exchange, its report alone marked mobile."
